<BaseLayout title="About | Md Arif Hossain" description="Academic background, combinatorial research, industrial analytics experience, and mathematical interests of Md Arif Hossain.">
 <div class="container page-shell"><header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">BACKGROUND / JOURNEY</p><h1>Curiosity about mathematics. <em>Motivation to apply it.</em></h1><p class="page-lead">I began in pure and computational mathematics and found a new set of questions in industrial systems: how can models allocate scarce resources, anticipate uncertainty, and help organizations make better decisions?</p></header>
  <section class="content-section two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">AT A GLANCE</p><h2>About me</h2></div><div class="prose-block"><p>I am <strong>Md Arif Hossain</strong>, a Mathematics graduate from Shahjalal University of Science and Technology (SUST), Bangladesh, and a Business Intelligence Analyst with INDESORE Group.</p><p>At SUST, I worked on computational methods for <strong>partially ordered sets and lattices</strong> and completed an undergraduate thesis on determinants, inverses, and eigenvalues of infinite matrices. Those experiences helped shape my interest in rigorous mathematical analysis and computation.</p><p>In professional practice, I have worked with production planning, Standard Minute Value estimation, capacity feasibility, efficiency, and operational decision support. Seeing the constraints and uncertainty of real manufacturing operations has deepened my interest in <strong>operations research, mixed-integer programming, and large-scale optimization</strong>.</p><p>I am interested in pursuing PhD research that connects mathematical theory, algorithms, and practical decision-making in manufacturing and supply-chain systems.</p></div></section>
  <section class="content-section"><p class="eyebrow">EDUCATION · RESEARCH · EXPERIENCE</p><h2>Selected milestones</h2><div class="timeline">{timeline.map(t=><article class="timeline-item"><p class="timeline-year">{t.period}</p><div><span class="mini-label">{t.label}</span><h3>{t.title}</h3><p class="muted">{t.sub}</p><p>{t.copy}</p></div></article>)}</div></section>
  <section class="content-section two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">UNDERGRADUATE THESIS</p><h2>Numerical & computational mathematics</h2></div><div class="prose-block"><h3>On the Determinant, Inverse, and Eigenvalues of Infinite Matrices</h3><p>My undergraduate thesis studied matrix determinants, inverse constructions, eigenvalues, matrix logarithms, convergence, and series-expansion methods in the setting of infinite matrices. The work included numerical approaches to approximating matrix-related quantities.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/research/">See research experience ↗</a></div></section>
  <section class="content-section two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">BEYOND RESEARCH</p><h2>Speedcubing & mathematical puzzles</h2></div><div class="prose-block"><p>Speedcubing sparked my interest in the relationship between mathematical structure and computational problem-solving. I served as Instructor & Head of the Cubing and Puzzle Wing at SUST Science Arena (February 2023–March 2024), organizing workshops and mentoring students.</p><ul>{awards.map(a=><li>{a}</li>)}</ul><p>In 2023, I co-presented a contributory talk on the Rubik’s Cube as an application of group theory.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/blog/">Explore mathematical writing ↗</a></div></section>
